1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,193
When they buried Margorie McCall,
an expensive ring was still on her finger.

2
00:00:04,655 --> 00:00:07,975
Her husband had tried to take it off,
but her finger was too swollen.

3
00:00:08,273 --> 00:00:10,158
Margorie had died of a fever,

4
00:00:10,188 --> 00:00:13,556
and her family rushed the burial,
afraid the illness might spread.

5
00:00:14,091 --> 00:00:17,406
That very night, while the earth
on her grave was still loose,

6
00:00:17,436 --> 00:00:18,793
thieves came to the graveyard.

7
00:00:19,091 --> 00:00:20,447
They knew about the ring.

8
00:00:20,764 --> 00:00:22,993
They opened the coffin
and tried to pull it off,

9
00:00:23,127 --> 00:00:24,084
but it wouldn't budge.

10
00:00:24,545 --> 00:00:26,193
So one of them pulled out a knife:

11
00:00:26,545 --> 00:00:29,247
if he couldn't remove the ring,
he would cut off her finger.

12
00:00:29,545 --> 00:00:31,120
The blade touched her skin.

13
00:00:31,509 --> 00:00:32,793
And at that very moment,

14
00:00:33,036 --> 00:00:36,575
the woman they believed was dead
sat up in the coffin and screamed.

15
00:00:37,036 --> 00:00:38,825
The thieves ran for their lives,

16
00:00:38,855 --> 00:00:42,320
while Margorie climbed out of the grave
and walked home in her burial clothes.

17
00:00:42,618 --> 00:00:45,793
Her husband was sitting with their children
when someone knocked at the door.

18
00:00:46,291 --> 00:00:47,393
He froze and said,

19
00:00:47,757 --> 00:00:50,956
“If your mother were still alive,
I'd swear that was her knock.”

20
00:00:51,327 --> 00:00:52,320
He opened the door.

21
00:00:52,855 --> 00:00:55,738
There stood Margorie,
in the clothes she'd been buried in,

22
00:00:55,982 --> 00:00:57,193
with blood on her hand.

23
00:00:57,727 --> 00:01:01,120
When he saw his wife, he clutched his chest
and dropped dead.

24
00:01:01,418 --> 00:01:04,370
A few days later, they buried him
in the very coffin

25
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:05,684
Margorie had climbed out of.

26
00:01:06,291 --> 00:01:09,829
She lived for many more years,
married again, and had children.

27
00:01:10,291 --> 00:01:13,756
And when her own time came,
these words were carved on her headstone:

28
00:01:14,364 --> 00:01:16,375
“Lived once, buried twice.”
